# 11. Linux Package Management

Ubuntu uses APT for package management.

## Update package information

```bash
sudo apt update
```

This refreshes local package information from configured repositories.

## Upgrade installed packages

```bash
sudo apt upgrade
```

This installs newer versions of installed packages when available.

## Install a package

```bash
sudo apt install package-name
```

Example:

```bash
sudo apt install tree
```

## Remove a package

```bash
sudo apt remove package-name
```

### Key Difference

```text
apt update
→ Refresh package information

apt upgrade
→ Upgrade installed packages

apt install
→ Install software

apt remove
→ Remove software
```

