# 12. Linux Archive Management

## `tar`

`tar` is used to create and extract archives containing files and directories.

### Create an archive

```bash
tar -cvf backup.tar folder/
```

### Extract an archive

```bash
tar -xvf backup.tar
```

### Create a gzip-compressed archive

```bash
tar -czvf backup.tar.gz folder/
```

### Extract a gzip-compressed archive

```bash
tar -xzvf backup.tar.gz
```

### Important

`tar` itself creates an archive. Compression can be added through options such as `-z`.

