# 28. Professional Behavioral Answer

## Question

**How do you approach troubleshooting when you do not immediately know the cause?**

### Answer

> I first gather information by asking targeted questions and understanding the symptoms. I then identify possible causes and start with the simplest and safest troubleshooting steps. I use available system tools, logs, and documentation to collect evidence rather than guessing. Once I identify the likely cause and have authorization to make the change, I apply the appropriate fix and verify the result with the user. Finally, I document the troubleshooting and resolution, or escalate the issue with my findings if it requires additional access or expertise.

